ivy: QA flagged our Java/Kotlin sample app: under spotty mobile networks + Android 15 we see streaming requests suddenly 504 after a token refresh. repro on Pixel and emulator with network toggles.

sam: do we still call token refresh from an interceptor synchronously? that pattern tends to chew dispatcher threads.

ivy: yes. TokenInterceptor calls refreshBlocking() which uses the same Retrofit/OkHttp client. snippet: 
```kotlin
override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
  var token = tokenStore.get()
  if (token == null) {
    synchronized(lock) {
      if (tokenStore.get() == null) tokenStore.set(refreshBlocking())
      token = tokenStore.get()
    }
  }
  val req = chain.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization", "Bearer $token").build()
  val resp = chain.proceed(req)
  if (resp.code == 401) {
    synchronized(lock) { tokenStore.set(refreshBlocking()) }
    return chain.proceed(req.newBuilder().header("Authorization", "Bearer ${tokenStore.get()}").build())
  }
  return resp
}
```

nate: yep classic re-entrancy + thundering herd. On Android 15 the HTTP/2 behaviour changed and pooled connections can lock up the dispatcher more visibly, turning slowdowns into 504s.

sdk-eng: short advice we should add to sample README and SDK docs: (1) do not call same OkHttp client from inside interceptor/authenticator; (2) use a small dedicated NoAuth client for token endpoint; (3) de-dupe refreshes (singleflight) and backoff on rate limit.

sam: we patched our app by: 
- creating refreshClient = OkHttpClient.Builder().apply { dispatcher(Dispatcher().apply { maxRequests = 2; maxRequestsPerHost = 1 }); connectionPool(ConnectionPool(0,1,TimeUnit.MINUTES)) }.build()
- refreshBlocking() uses refreshClient and is non-blocking wrt main pool
- added singleflight: Kotlin Mutex + Deferred for coroutine apps, AtomicReference<CompletableFuture> for Java

ivy: implemented and QA reports the repro disappears. also added setRetryOnConnectionFailure(false) for streaming endpoints and lowered maxRequestsPerHost on main client.

nate: can we add a tiny Java snippet for the CompletableFuture singleflight to the samples folder? I can convert to Kotlin afterwards. gist: 
```java
private final AtomicReference<CompletableFuture<Token>> inflight = new AtomicReference<>();
public Token refreshSingleflight() {
  for (;;) {
    CompletableFuture<Token> cur = inflight.get();
    if (cur != null) return cur.join();
    CompletableFuture<Token> f = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> refreshBlocking());
    if (inflight.compareAndSet(null, f)) {
      try { return f.join(); } finally { inflight.compareAndSet(f, null); }
    }
  }
}
```

sdk-eng: add an integration test that fires 20 parallel requests with the token expired, then toggles airplane mode; mark it as flaky and optional in CI for real devices. Also add a short README callout about Android 15 HTTP/2 prioritization changes so engineers understand why this surfaced now.

ivY: (typo) I'll open PR with sample changes + test + docs. I'll also include a short migration note: "If you previously relied on blocking refresh inside interceptor, switch to separate refresh client + singleflight." :memo: :rocket:

